    "10": {
      "type": "Content",
      "is_root": "0",
      "node_name": "claude.md",
      "page_title": "claude.md",
      "content": "# claude.md - Main Intake (tree 142849578)\n\n## Purpose\nPersonal-injury law-firm phone intake for receptionists/agents. Greets the caller, captures the situation on ONE screen, routes to the right outcome, collects contact info, and books a consultation or callback. Capture-only (no API/CX Actions).\n\n## Architecture (rebuilt Jul 2026 - button-nav replaced by one screen + script + router)\n- 1 Personal Injury Intake (Content, ROOT): empathy + all questions as NATIVE conditional form fields. proceed_mode always shown; case_type/event_date/injured/medical_treatment shown when proceed_mode == 'Proceed with questions'; case-specific fields shown by case_type. One Continue button -> 8.\n- 8 Evaluate Intake and Route (Script): reads the fields (direct value match, no normalization), sets the single boolean needs_review_offer, stages review_offer_html + intake_summary_html/_text. -> 9.\n- 9 Route Caller (Scoring router, advanced_logic_node=1): 'needs_review_offer == true' -> 6; empty default -> 2.\n- 6 Attorney Review Offer (Content, SHARED): renders ${transforms.review_offer_html} (SOL / no-injury / liability-unclear / other message staged by the script). Yes -> 2; No -> 7.\n- 2 Collect Caller Information (Content): shows ${transforms.intake_summary_html} + a copy-to-clipboard case note; native name/phone/email fields. Collected -> 3; declines -> 7.\n- 3 Schedule Consultation (Content): scheduled -> 4; needs callback -> 5.\n- 4 Appointment Confirmed / 5 Callback Scheduled / 7 End of Call: terminals.\n\n## Data dictionary\nForm variables (each defined ONCE on node 1): proceed_mode, case_type, event_date, injured, medical_treatment, at_fault, insurance_status, incident_location, provider_licensed, harm_negligence, work_related, reported_employer; plus name, phone, email (node 2).\nScript-set boolean: needs_review_offer (the only flag the router tests). The four review reasons (SOL / no-injury / liability / other) are locals in node 8 that only pick the message; they are not exported.\nTransforms: review_offer_html, intake_summary_html, intake_summary_text.\n\n## Routing logic (in node 8, priority order mirrors the old flow)\nOnly when proceed_mode == 'Proceed with questions': Other -> review(other); Workers Comp & not work related -> review(other); event_date 'More than 2 years ago' -> review(SOL); Auto/Slip & 'No one was injured' -> review(no injury); Auto & fault 'Unclear...' -> review(liability); Med Mal & harm 'No' -> review(liability); else -> Collect. Fast-track proceed modes skip questions -> Collect.\n\n## Conventions & gotchas\n- merge_vars_not_fixed = '1' (REQUIRED): node 6 & 2 render script-staged ${transforms.*}; without this the first-rendered value would stick.\n- Native selects submit the OPTION TEXT as value; the eval script matches on that text directly (no normalization).\n- Router tests only the script-set boolean needs_review_offer (never raw form values).\n- No duplicate variables and no duplicate buttons: every question is one native field; the old repeated 'When/Injured/Treatment' screens and duplicated date/injury buttons are gone.\n- ASCII only (hyphens, not em dashes).\n\n## Changelog\n- 2026-07-17 - Brent (rebuild via zingtree-workflow-builder) - Replaced button navigation (26 nodes, duplicated eventDate/injured/medicalTreatment/eventLoc vars and repeated date/injury buttons) with one intake screen (native conditional fields) -> Evaluate Intake and Route script -> Route Caller router. Collapsed old outcome screens 95/96/97/50 into one shared Attorney Review Offer node. Kept Collect/Schedule/Confirmed/Callback/End. Added claude.md node.\n- 2026-07-21 \u00b7 Brent via Claude (improve for import) \u00b7 verification pass, no structural changes needed. Confirmed: import lint clean; script node 100 passes node --check; all 11 routing string-comparisons map exactly to the select option text (normalized); router 101 tests only `needs_review_offer == true` with empty fallback; merge_vars_not_fixed=1 for the shared review/collect nodes.\n- 2026-07-21 \u00b7 Brent via Claude (route coherence fix) \u00b7 node 100 was exporting four route_* form flags (route_other/route_sol/route_no_injury/route_liability) that NO router tested -- implied 5 routes when node 101 only branches on needs_review_offer (->95 review offer) vs default (->90 collect info). Removed the four dead setFormData exports; the four checks remain as locals that select the review message (review_offer_html) shown on the one shared node 95. Behavior unchanged (matches the original tree's convergence); logic now reads honestly. Nodes touched: 100, 1000.\n- 2026-07-21 \u00b7 Brent via Claude (lean-code rewrite) \u00b7 rewrote node 100 to the new \"Zingtree is already safe / plain minimal code\" rule: dropped the norm() helper and all input normalization (match native select values directly), removed esc() (intake fields are fixed-value selects), collapsed the four route_* locals into one `reason` string. Same behavior, far less ceremony. Nodes touched: 100, 1000.\n- 2026-07-21 \u00b7 Brent via Claude (sequential renumber) \u00b7 compacted node IDs to a gapless 1..N sequence (lowest-available rule). Map: 2->1 90->2 91->3 92->4 93->5 95->6 99->7 100->8 101->9 1000->10. Updated root_node_id, is_root, all links/continuations, and the claude.md node map. Scripts unaffected (no node IDs in code).",
